1
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,800
"Blue Lips"

2
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,700
(Episode 8)

3
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,920
Did you guys sleep together last night?

4
00:01:16,099 --> 00:01:17,500
I already told you.

5
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:19,619
I'm not interested in men.

6
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:22,400
Fine.

7
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,400
I see you're refusing the easy way out,

8
00:01:24,659 --> 00:01:25,819
so you gotta go the hard way.

9
00:01:26,739 --> 00:01:27,739
Hey, buddy.

10
00:01:28,199 --> 00:01:29,940
Violence doesn't solve anything.

11
00:01:30,639 --> 00:01:31,840
Let's talk this out calmly.

12
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,015
This is none of your business.

13
00:01:34,039 --> 00:01:35,039
Stay out of it.

14
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:36,480
Xiao Wu is my friend.

15
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,500
His business

16
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,860
is my business.

17
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:41,759
You don't need to explain anything to him.

18
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,440
What exactly happened?

19
00:01:43,659 --> 00:01:44,939
Let me help you figure this out.

20
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Come on.

21
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,840
My boyfriend cheated on me.

22
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:50,840
And the guy was wearing blue lipstick.

23
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,500
Blue lipstick, sure.

24
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,936
But his hat is pulled down so low,

25
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:55,080
you can't even see his face.

26
00:01:55,539 --> 00:01:56,976
What day of the week did you take this?

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Last Wednesday.

28
00:01:58,780 --> 00:01:59,780
That explains it.

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,539
Xiao Wu here

30
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:02,519
doesn't sing at the Blue
Moon Bar on Wednesdays.

31
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:04,219
Everyone at the bar can vouch for that.

32
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,598
You said your boyfriend

33
00:02:05,599 --> 00:02:06,995
went out with someone from the bar.

34
00:02:07,019 --> 00:02:08,379
Then it definitely wasn't Xiao Wu.

35
00:02:12,179 --> 00:02:13,179
Fine.

36
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:15,480
If you're lying to me,

37
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,300
you'll pay for it.

38
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,280
Are you okay?

39
00:02:27,615 --> 00:02:29,826
I don't even know the guy
he was just talking about.

40
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:30,199
I...

41
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:31,820
I know.

42
00:02:32,199 --> 00:02:33,400
You're not into men, right?

43
00:02:36,752 --> 00:02:37,351
I have to praise you.

44
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,900
You did well today.

45
00:02:39,199 --> 00:02:40,460
You actually defended yourself,

46
00:02:40,559 --> 00:02:41,759
and didn't even throw a punch.

47
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:43,279
No...

48
00:02:43,539 --> 00:02:44,559
from now on at the bar,

49
00:02:44,739 --> 00:02:46,459
things like this will happen more and more.

50
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,440
Fighting won't solve the problem.

51
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,260
Stop always trying to fight people.

52
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,760
What is your brain for?

53
00:02:52,119 --> 00:02:53,119
What is your mouth for?

54
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:54,780
Learn to use them.

55
00:02:57,679 --> 00:02:59,359
It's not like you won't be around anymore.

56
00:02:59,739 --> 00:03:01,379
Are you going to stop
looking out for me?

57
00:03:04,519 --> 00:03:05,619
That's not what I meant.

58
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,079
What I mean is,

59
00:03:07,219 --> 00:03:08,379
you can't always count on me.

60
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,679
I'm not going to be by your side 24/7.

61
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,440
What will you do when I'm not around?

62
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,820
You need to be able to
solve problems on your own.

63
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:17,079
That's how you can better protect yourself.

64
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,880
Right?

65
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:22,639
Dummy.

66
00:03:33,739 --> 00:03:34,739
Xiao Wu.

67
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,039
You're here so early today.

68
00:03:36,199 --> 00:03:37,279
We haven't even opened yet.

69
00:03:38,599 --> 00:03:39,718
Did Brother Mo

70
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,880
leave with you yesterday?

71
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,800
Why?

72
00:03:46,539 --> 00:03:47,539
Nothing really.

73
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:49,359
It's just that when we
were closing up yesterday,

74
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,360
he came looking for you.

75
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,159
He didn't see you,

76
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,240
and even asked me about it.

77
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:53,340
Then,

78
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,119
I turned around and he was gone.

79
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:56,460
So I just wanted to ask you.

80
00:04:02,039 --> 00:04:03,619
Are you and Brother Mo

81
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:05,380
really together?

82
00:04:11,239 --> 00:04:11,519
No.

83
00:04:11,639 --> 00:04:13,320
What's there to be shy about?

84
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,699
We can all see it.

85
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,079
Wait.

86
00:04:18,219 --> 00:04:19,219
You guys?

87
00:04:20,159 --> 00:04:21,159
Who else?

88
00:04:21,679 --> 00:04:22,679
Well, me,

89
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,500
Xiao Fu,

90
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:25,300
Xiao Lee,

91
00:04:25,639 --> 00:04:26,639
Ah Yuan...

92
00:04:27,139 --> 00:04:28,139
A lot of people.

93
00:04:30,599 --> 00:04:30,980
I mean,

94
00:04:31,119 --> 00:04:33,139
Brother Mo hangs out here every single day.

95
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:35,140
If you ask him, he won't admit it,

96
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,599
but who couldn't tell?

97
00:04:37,659 --> 00:04:38,079
Well,
maybe he just

98
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:41,679
likes coming here to
drink and listen to music.

99
00:04:43,219 --> 00:04:45,899
Would he pay your damages just
for drinking and listening to music?

100
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:47,980
Damages?

101
00:04:49,059 --> 00:04:50,059
What damages?

102
00:04:50,139 --> 00:04:50,920
You didn't know?
Remember last time

103
00:04:51,901 --> 00:04:53,135
when Brother Hao came and caused a scene?

104
00:04:53,159 --> 00:04:54,300
You guys got into a fight.

105
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:55,960
Originally,

106
00:04:55,961 --> 00:04:57,279
you and Brother Hao were supposed to

107
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,480
split the cost of the damages.

108
00:04:58,739 --> 00:05:00,639
But Brother Mo paid your share.

109
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:02,500
He said he was involved in the fight too,

110
00:05:02,659 --> 00:05:03,659
So he covered the cost?

111
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:06,440
You really didn't know?

112
00:05:10,559 --> 00:05:11,559
Then I've said too much.

113
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,199
How much did he pay?

114
00:05:18,139 --> 00:05:19,139
Not that much.

115
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:21,780
Guan Zhenghao was supposed
to pay the lion's share anyway.

116
00:05:23,079 --> 00:05:24,079
But,

117
00:05:24,119 --> 00:05:26,239
Brother Mo is really good to you.

118
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:27,699
He's so protective of you.

119
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,719
I've known him for a long time,

120
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:32,760
and I've never seen him with any friends.

121
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,760
He's always been a lone wolf.

122
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:37,259
I really didn't expect

123
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,880
he'd go this far for you.

124
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:54,380
What's up?

125
00:05:54,639 --> 00:05:55,760
Here to buy Vandacon?

126
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,559
It's not time yet, is it?

127
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:05,920
What's this about?

128
00:06:10,719 --> 00:06:12,199
These things are too expensive.

129
00:06:13,099 --> 00:06:14,099
I can't accept them.

130
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:15,900
Besides,

131
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,680
the compensation for the fight

132
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,740
shouldn't have been paid by you.

133
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,119
We both got into that fight.

134
00:06:24,639 --> 00:06:26,319
It's not right to make you pay for it all.

135
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,100
The phone and watch
haven't even been opened.

136
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,680
I wouldn't feel right keeping them.

137
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,500
What about the money?

138
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,640
You're still so short on cash.

139
00:06:43,179 --> 00:06:44,099
Where did this money come from?

140
00:06:44,179 --> 00:06:45,339
That's none of your business.

141
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,300
Where's your guitar?

142
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,500
I sold it.

143
00:06:57,179 --> 00:06:57,940
Why did you sell it?

144
00:06:58,199 --> 00:06:59,219
Just to pay me back?

145
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,959
Haven't I told you that I...

146
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:01,960
I know.

147
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,800
You said it.

148
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:06,300
With our relationship,

149
00:07:06,301 --> 00:07:08,181
it's only natural for you
to spend money on me.

150
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,238
But I don't want our relationship

151
00:07:10,239 --> 00:07:11,820
to be so deeply tied to money.

152
00:07:16,179 --> 00:07:17,179
What do you mean?

153
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:18,980
You want to settle the score with me?

154
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,659
I just don't want to owe you too much.

155
00:07:26,239 --> 00:07:28,279
Because I'm afraid I won't
be able to pay you back.

156
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:33,135
I don't need you to pay me back.

157
00:07:33,159 --> 00:07:34,320
I did it willingly.

158
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,460
Really?

159
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,780
Then why did you spend so much money on me?

160
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,480
I...

161
00:07:46,639 --> 00:07:47,659
It's because...

162
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,360
Because of what?

163
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,480
Is it just because

164
00:07:57,559 --> 00:07:58,840
you want to sleep with me?

165
00:07:59,599 --> 00:08:00,599
Right?

166
00:08:10,039 --> 00:08:11,959
Well, if you don't want
these things, then fine.

167
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
I'm leaving.

168
00:08:20,293 --> 00:08:21,653
I still have a gig at Blue Moon.

169
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,860
How are you going to
play without your guitar?

170
00:08:25,439 --> 00:08:26,439
The guitar is gone,

171
00:08:26,899 --> 00:08:27,899
but I'm still here.

172
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,340
Besides,

173
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:33,220
no one will complain
about the noise anymore.

174
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:38,340
Wait a minute.

175
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:43,460
This is a women's watch.

176
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:45,319
It's of no use to me.

177
00:08:47,859 --> 00:08:49,099
I don't know who to give it to.

178
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,760
You keep it.

179
00:08:56,979 --> 00:08:57,979
Or throw it away.

180
00:10:02,119 --> 00:10:02,640
What's wrong?

181
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,880
You're not at the shop.

182
00:10:03,881 --> 00:10:05,201
Just wandering the streets alone.

183
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:07,579
Bored.

184
00:10:07,699 --> 00:10:08,699
Getting some fresh air.

185
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,319
You're in a bad mood.

186
00:10:13,199 --> 00:10:13,800
Get in.

187
00:10:14,079 --> 00:10:15,316
I happen to be in a bad mood too.

188
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:16,340
Let's chat.

189
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,619
Just looking at you,

190
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:38,319
I can tell you're troubled by love.

191
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:43,100
But I'm in no position to judge.

192
00:10:47,119 --> 00:10:48,119
So?

193
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:51,220
You get troubled by love too?

194
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,220
Back then, I just couldn't let it go.

195
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,180
I kept the person,

196
00:10:57,319 --> 00:10:58,519
but couldn't keep their heart.

197
00:10:58,659 --> 00:11:00,299
I ended up making a total fool of myself.

198
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,020
It's better to just let go.

199
00:11:02,979 --> 00:11:04,739
There's no need to
drag it out for too long.

200
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,600
Here.

201
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:47,920
Hello?

202
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,600
Are you free today?

203
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,800
I want to see you.

204
00:11:56,579 --> 00:11:57,880
I don't think I can today.

205
00:12:01,439 --> 00:12:02,439
What about later tonight?

206
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,279
Shixian.

207
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:06,520
Who's calling?

208
00:12:10,319 --> 00:12:11,319
The bar owner.

209
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:13,840
Asking if I can work tonight.

210
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:20,420
Hello?

211
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,520
I really can't make it today.

212
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,500
What about tomorrow?

213
00:12:32,739 --> 00:12:34,479
Probably not for the next couple of days.

214
00:12:39,859 --> 00:12:40,859
Okay.

215
00:12:41,439 --> 00:12:42,439
Wu Shixian.

216
00:12:44,319 --> 00:12:45,760
I want to ask you a question.

217
00:12:52,359 --> 00:12:53,520
In your eyes,

218
00:12:56,079 --> 00:12:57,239
what exactly am I to you?

219
00:13:03,859 --> 00:13:04,859
A...

220
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,520
really good...

221
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,600
brother.

222
00:13:12,739 --> 00:13:13,739
Never mind.

223
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:14,600
I'll let you go.

224
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:15,960
I won't bother you anymore.

225
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,520
I'm hanging up.

226
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:24,220
Shixian.

227
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Let's go.

228
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,560
Ah Heng.

229
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:23,520
Do me a favor.

230
00:14:23,979 --> 00:14:25,835
I'll be busy lately, so I
won't be coming around.

231
00:14:25,859 --> 00:14:26,859
Help me give this

232
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,460
to Wu Shixian.

233
00:14:31,239 --> 00:14:32,239
What is this?

234
00:14:32,659 --> 00:14:33,659
A cash gift.

235
00:14:35,539 --> 00:14:36,539
Seriously?

236
00:14:36,619 --> 00:14:37,319
I'm kidding.

237
00:14:37,619 --> 00:14:38,779
You believe everything I say.

238
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:41,079
I was gonna say.

239
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,520
He's so cool,

240
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:44,420
there's no way he'd get married this young.

241
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,920
Any message you want me to pass on?

242
00:14:53,479 --> 00:14:54,979
Tell him to live a good life.

243
00:15:48,779 --> 00:15:49,779
Hello?

244
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:52,779
What?

245
00:15:53,239 --> 00:15:54,239
Which hospital?

246
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:57,779
Okay, I'll be right there.

247
00:16:53,079 --> 00:16:53,600
Doctor,

248
00:16:54,039 --> 00:16:55,039
how is she?

249
00:16:55,739 --> 00:16:59,199
Sudden syncope in patients with pulmonary
arterial hypertension is a normal occurrence.

250
00:16:59,239 --> 00:17:00,500
She's stabilized now.

251
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:01,520
However,

252
00:17:01,659 --> 00:17:03,278
the patient is showing
signs of right heart failure,

253
00:17:03,279 --> 00:17:04,839
which needs to be taken very seriously.

254
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:08,222
This episode was triggered
by chronic fatigue and a cold.

255
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:09,420
It's still quite dangerous.

256
00:17:54,319 --> 00:17:56,879
The patient has been relying on
medication for treatment, right?

257
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,380
Yes.

258
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:00,539
Given her current condition,

259
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,840
medication alone probably won't be enough.

260
00:18:03,079 --> 00:18:04,658
You should take her to a
major hospital's outpatient clinic

261
00:18:04,659 --> 00:18:05,739
for a thorough examination.

262
00:18:06,199 --> 00:18:08,439
There are many types of
pulmonary arterial hypertension.

263
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:12,156
You need to see a specialist as soon as
possible to determine the exact classification.

264
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,180
Okay.

265
00:18:13,279 --> 00:18:14,279
I understand.

266
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,915
I remember what you like to drink.

267
00:18:42,939 --> 00:18:43,460
Wait for me a sec.

268
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:44,680
Xiao Wu.

269
00:18:47,539 --> 00:18:47,920
This...

270
00:18:48,399 --> 00:18:49,519
Brother Mo gave this to you.

271
00:18:51,319 --> 00:18:52,420
When did he give it to you?

272
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:54,720
The day before yesterday.

273
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,100
You weren't here then,

274
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,380
so he asked me to...

275
00:18:59,579 --> 00:19:00,579
Where is he?

276
00:19:02,420 --> 00:19:03,420
I don't know.

277
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:08,060
He said...

278
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,140
you should live a good life.

279
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:30,680
Hello.

280
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:33,979
The number you have dialed
is temporarily unavailable.

281
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:43,520
Teng Mo.

282
00:21:58,979 --> 00:21:59,979
Get up.

283
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:01,460
It's time to change the sheets.

284
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:02,800
There's no rush.

285
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:05,080
Let me hold you a little longer.

286
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:11,420
Shixian.

287
00:22:13,859 --> 00:22:15,460
Don't trust anyone from now on.

288
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:16,859
People nowadays

289
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,060
might look decent on the outside,

290
00:22:19,979 --> 00:22:21,779
but they're rotten to
the core on the inside.

291
00:22:22,239 --> 00:22:23,239
Including me.

292
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,040
I'm not as good as you think.

293
00:22:28,859 --> 00:22:30,979
You've been talking
weirdly for a while now.

294
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:33,779
Are these your dying words?

295
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,640
What are you talking about?

296
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:38,739
I just think you're sweet,

297
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:39,899
and I care about you.

298
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:42,039
This is for you.

299
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:43,560
What is this?

300
00:22:48,579 --> 00:22:49,739
Look at it when you get back.
